{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423741","formula":"C₁₃H₂₀N₂O₂","hill":"C13H20N2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":20.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Procaine","ru":"Прокаин","uk":"Прокаїн"},"descriptions":{"en":"Procaine is a local anesthetic drug of the amino ester group. It is most commonly used in dental procedures to numb the area around a tooth and is also used to reduce the pain of intramuscular injection of penicillin. Owing to the ubiquity of the trade name Novocain (without the \"e\" in the original German patent) or Novocaine (with the \"e\" in the US patent), in some regions, procaine is referred to generically as novocaine.","ru":"Прокаин (новокаин, гидрохлорид диэтиламиноэтилового эфира п-аминобензойной кислоты) — анестетик с умеренной активностью.","uk":"Новокаїн (прокаїн, β-диетиламіноетилового ефіру пара-амінобензойної кислоти гідрохлорид) — хімічна речовина з місцевою знеболювальною дією. Міжнародна назва англ. procaine."},"fame":41,"pubchemCid":4914,"mass":236.31,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCN(CC)CCOC(=O)C1=CC=C(C=C1)N","inchikey":"MFDFERRIHVXMIY-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(diethylamino)ethyl 4-aminobenzoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"4914","atoms":37,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.219,"y":-0.11,"z":-0.105,"el":"O"},{"x":0.564,"y":-2.138,"z":-0.861,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.893,"y":0.194,"z":-0.079,"el":"N"},{"x":5.892,"y":1.15,"z":0.493,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.497,"y":0.586,"z":0.116,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.787,"y":1.295,"z":0.278,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.205,"y":-0.995,"z":0.713,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.561,"y":-0.539,"z":-0.294,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.477,"y":2.54,"z":-0.536,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.634,"y":-1.453,"z":0.476,"el":"C"},{"x":0.749,"y":-1.011,"z":-0.429,"el":"C"},{"x":2.099,"y":-0.443,"z":-0.185,"el":"C"},{"x":3.129,"y":-1.295,"z":0.1